1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,800
Hi, big guy.

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:07,125
That must be Rita Mae.

3
00:00:07,125 --> 00:00:08,294
She sure got here quickly.

4
00:00:08,294 --> 00:00:13,989
That's a good sign.

5
00:00:13,989 --> 00:00:23,824
She must like you and your work, Marilyn.

6
00:00:23,824 --> 00:01:00,759
I think she's just anxious to see Max.

7
00:01:00,759 --> 00:01:01,609
She loves children.

8
00:01:01,609 --> 00:01:02,109
Hi, Marilyn.

9
00:01:02,109 --> 00:01:02,359
Welcome.

10
00:01:02,359 --> 00:01:04,182
It's so nice of you to come.

11
00:01:04,182 --> 00:01:22,738
Oh, I just wanted to see your baby, Max.

12
00:01:22,738 --> 00:01:23,716
Hello, Rita Mae.

13
00:01:23,716 --> 00:01:26,050
I haven't seen you since the hospital.

14
00:01:26,050 --> 00:01:31,115
I'm Ellen Stewart, Marilyn's mother-in-law.

15
00:01:31,115 --> 00:01:33,517
We met at the hospital.

16
00:01:33,517 --> 00:01:34,567
How are you?

17
00:01:34,567 --> 00:01:35,795
How are you?

18
00:01:35,795 --> 00:01:39,933
Oh, and there is Max!

19
00:01:39,933 --> 00:01:44,229
Oh! My, how he's grown!

20
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:47,207
A little present for Max.

21
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:51,435
Oh, it's beautiful, Rita Mae!

22
00:01:51,435 --> 00:01:52,518
You shouldn't have.

23
00:01:52,518 --> 00:01:53,163
It's nothing.

24
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:55,163
It's just a little present for Max.

25
00:01:55,163 --> 00:01:58,740
Can I get you some coffee or tea or a cold drink, Rita Mae?

26
00:01:58,740 --> 00:01:59,828
Oh, nothing, thank you.

27
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:04,376
Well, I will leave you two to talk.

28
00:02:04,376 --> 00:02:08,385
Come on, you big guy.

29
00:02:08,385 --> 00:02:09,385
Yes, come on.

30
00:02:09,385 --> 00:02:10,052
That's it.

31
00:02:10,052 --> 00:02:11,195
It's nice seeing you.

32
00:02:11,195 --> 00:02:12,257
Let me know if you need anything.

33
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:13,030
Thanks, Ellen.

34
00:02:13,030 --> 00:02:16,986
Thanks, Ellen.

35
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:17,756
OK, Marilyn.

36
00:02:17,756 --> 00:02:20,204
You sounded like you've made a decision

37
00:02:20,204 --> 00:02:21,884
when you called me.

38
00:02:21,884 --> 00:02:23,692
I have made a decision, Rita Mae.

39
00:02:23,692 --> 00:02:28,872
I've decided to stay at home and be a full-time mother.

40
00:02:28,872 --> 00:02:30,898
I'm disappointed, but I respect your decision.

41
00:02:30,898 --> 00:02:32,996
If I had a child as cute as Max,

42
00:02:32,996 --> 00:02:34,676
I might do the same thing.

43
00:02:34,676 --> 00:02:36,181
But I haven't finished telling you

44
00:02:36,181 --> 00:02:37,832
the other half of my decision.

45
00:02:37,832 --> 00:02:38,957
The other half?

46
00:02:38,957 --> 00:02:39,332
Yes.

47
00:02:39,332 --> 00:02:41,710
I think I can stay at home

48
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:45,208
and take care of Max and continue my career.

49
00:02:45,208 --> 00:02:46,766
Sounds interesting.

50
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:49,744
Let me hear it.

51
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:50,494
Do you remember

52
00:02:50,494 --> 00:02:52,722
our talks about custom-designed dresses for the boutique?

53
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:54,722
I sure do.

54
00:02:54,722 --> 00:02:58,678
Why can't I design dresses for you here at home?

55
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:00,678
And make them here.

56
00:03:00,678 --> 00:03:01,656
Have the fittings here, too.

57
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:04,634
And I could do the selling and the pricing at the boutique.

58
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:05,347
Exactly.

59
00:03:05,347 --> 00:03:06,061
Oh!

60
00:03:06,061 --> 00:03:09,041
What kind of dresses would you design?

61
00:03:09,041 --> 00:03:12,732
I've thought about that for some time.

62
00:03:12,732 --> 00:03:13,160
Yes?

63
00:03:13,160 --> 00:03:16,545
Wedding dresses.

64
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:17,625
Wedding dresses?

65
00:03:17,625 --> 00:03:19,523
Brilliant idea!

66
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:24,341
There's a big market today in wedding dresses.

67
00:03:24,341 --> 00:03:25,479
That's what I thought.

68
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:27,279
I like the idea very much.

69
00:03:27,279 --> 00:03:28,457
And if it's successful,

70
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:31,435
we can expand to all kinds of dresses.

71
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:32,768
That's what I thought.

72
00:03:32,768 --> 00:03:35,163
As a matter of fact,

73
00:03:35,163 --> 00:03:37,391
I have a customer for your first wedding dress.

74
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:38,641
My niece is getting married,

75
00:03:38,641 --> 00:03:42,569
and I've been trying to find just the right thing for her.

76
00:03:42,569 --> 00:03:46,042
Marilyn, you're going to design my niece's dress. Marilyn

77
00:03:46,042 --> 00:03:46,885
That'll be our first one,

78
00:03:46,885 --> 00:03:49,303
and then we'll use it to sell others.

79
00:03:49,303 --> 00:03:51,303
Do you really mean it?

80
00:03:51,303 --> 00:03:52,281
I really mean it.

81
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:55,592
It's a simple idea, and it will work.

82
00:03:55,592 --> 00:03:57,259
You can certainly design dresses.

83
00:03:57,259 --> 00:03:58,237
I know that.

84
00:03:58,237 --> 00:04:01,215
And there's no reason why you can't do it from your home.

85
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:02,325
I'm so excited!

86
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:05,193
I can't wait to tell Richard!

87
00:04:05,193 --> 00:04:07,171
If I had a baby like Max,

88
00:04:07,171 --> 00:04:11,149
I'd want to stay home and be near him all the time, too.

89
00:04:11,149 --> 00:04:12,578
You're making the right decision

90
00:04:12,578 --> 00:04:16,105
for Max and for yourself too, Marilyn.

91
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:17,945
It all sounds so easy.

92
00:04:17,945 --> 00:04:19,750
Now the hard work begins.

93
00:04:19,750 --> 00:04:20,750
Would you like

94
00:04:20,750 --> 00:04:23,460
to see some of my designs that I've been working on?

95
00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:25,038
I'd love to.

96
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:30,994
Ooh! Oh, that's wonderful!

97
00:04:30,994 --> 00:04:33,994
Ooh ...
